1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:37,017
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,017 --> 00:02:41,017
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:50,017
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:50,017 --> 00:02:53,017
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:53,017 --> 00:02:56,017
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,017 --> 00:02:59,017
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,017 --> 00:03:02,017
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,017
This sight!

10
00:03:06,017 --> 00:03:09,017
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:12,017
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:12,017 --> 00:03:17,017
the crew will come a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,017 --> 00:03:23,017
The Straw Hat Pirates were led to an uncharted island

14
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:28,017
while chasing a giant beetle Luffy insisted on recruiting to the team.

15
00:03:29,017 --> 00:03:31,017
All right, big guy, you're gonna join...

16
00:03:33,017 --> 00:03:34,017
Boss is with me!

17
00:03:35,017 --> 00:03:37,017
And he'd rather die than become...

18
00:03:38,017 --> 00:03:39,017
The Pirate!

19
00:03:42,017 --> 00:03:44,017
The beetle was in fact the guardian of Yoko,

20
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:47,017
a young girl who hates pirates.

21
00:03:47,017 --> 00:03:50,017
She was a member of a strange community known as...

22
00:03:50,017 --> 00:03:52,017
Consorn Island!

23
00:03:52,017 --> 00:03:55,017
Home away from home for expatriates of the East Blue!

24
00:03:55,017 --> 00:03:56,017
We like to call it...

25
00:03:56,017 --> 00:03:58,017
Little East Blue!

26
00:04:00,017 --> 00:04:01,017
Unbeknownst to the islanders,

27
00:04:01,017 --> 00:04:05,017
a vicious group known as the Amigo Pirates are headed their way,

28
00:04:05,017 --> 00:04:08,017
under the orders of the dreaded pirate, Shiki.

29
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:13,017
Special presentation related to the movie,

30
00:04:13,017 --> 00:04:15,017
Little East Blue in danger!

31
00:04:15,017 --> 00:04:18,017
I'd better keep it at a slow and safe speed.

32
00:04:18,017 --> 00:04:20,017
They've got an absurd amount of reefs out here.

33
00:04:20,017 --> 00:04:21,017
Ready, go!

34
00:04:21,017 --> 00:04:22,017
We love you, Nami!

35
00:04:22,017 --> 00:04:23,017
Huh?

36
00:04:23,017 --> 00:04:24,017
Over here!

37
00:04:24,017 --> 00:04:25,017
Right this way!

38
00:04:25,017 --> 00:04:26,017
A welcome party?

39
00:04:26,017 --> 00:04:27,017
I guess?

40
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,017
No!

41
00:04:28,017 --> 00:04:29,017
No!

42
00:04:29,017 --> 00:04:30,017
No!

43
00:04:30,017 --> 00:04:31,017
No!

44
00:04:31,017 --> 00:04:32,017
No!

45
00:04:32,017 --> 00:04:33,017
No!

46
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:34,017
No!

47
00:04:34,017 --> 00:04:35,017
No!

48
00:04:35,017 --> 00:04:36,017
No!

49
00:04:36,017 --> 00:04:37,017
No!

50
00:04:37,017 --> 00:04:38,017
No!

51
00:04:38,017 --> 00:04:39,017
No!

52
00:04:39,017 --> 00:04:40,017
No!

53
00:04:40,017 --> 00:04:41,017
No!

54
00:04:41,017 --> 00:04:42,017
No!

55
00:04:42,017 --> 00:04:43,017
No!

56
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:44,017
No!

57
00:04:44,017 --> 00:04:45,017
No!

58
00:04:45,017 --> 00:04:47,017
It's just one party, I guess?

59
00:04:51,017 --> 00:04:52,017
Guys!

60
00:04:52,017 --> 00:04:53,017
It's really her!

61
00:04:53,017 --> 00:04:55,017
We're in the presence of the real life Nami!

62
00:04:55,017 --> 00:04:58,017
And she's even cuter than a wanted poster!

63
00:04:58,017 --> 00:04:59,017
I can't stop the twos!

64
00:04:59,017 --> 00:05:01,017
I'm so happy to be alive!

65
00:05:01,017 --> 00:05:02,017
Yeah, yeah!

66
00:05:02,017 --> 00:05:03,017
Well, this is weird.

67
00:05:03,017 --> 00:05:05,017
Who are you guys?

68
00:05:05,017 --> 00:05:07,017
Wow, you actually care enough to ask!

69
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:09,017
We're the founders of the unofficial Nami Fan Club,

70
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:12,017
otherwise known as the Oranami Group!

71
00:05:12,017 --> 00:05:14,017
You're my Fan Club?

72
00:05:14,017 --> 00:05:18,057
We-L-O-V-E!

73
00:05:18,437 --> 00:05:20,597
You! You're the best, Nami!

74
00:05:22,477 --> 00:05:24,357
Stop it! You're grossing me out!

75
00:05:30,257 --> 00:05:32,917
Look, I need to see Luffy. Can you just take me to him?

76
00:05:33,157 --> 00:05:35,177
Of course! Anything you want, Nami!

77
00:05:36,617 --> 00:05:38,137
What an obnoxious day.

78
00:05:39,077 --> 00:05:41,537
And quit sucking up to me already. It's not working.

79
00:05:41,797 --> 00:05:43,017
Your wish is our command!

80
00:05:44,017 --> 00:05:48,717
Oh man, this is so much fun! You guys should try this!

81
00:05:49,257 --> 00:05:51,397
Well, I'm glad you're enjoying yourself.

82
00:05:54,037 --> 00:05:57,797
I'm sure this is nostalgic for you since you came from Fusha Village.

83
00:05:57,937 --> 00:06:01,337
Uh-huh. But all our windmills were pretty small compared to this one.

84
00:06:02,657 --> 00:06:06,677
We sort of consider that windmill the official landmark of Little East Blue,

85
00:06:06,857 --> 00:06:08,157
so we had to make an impression.

86
00:06:10,117 --> 00:06:12,277
See? Just like the dojo you grew up in.

87
00:06:12,277 --> 00:06:13,597
Huh.

88
00:06:20,157 --> 00:06:20,397
Huh?

89
00:06:20,397 --> 00:06:20,657
Huh?

90
00:06:20,657 --> 00:06:38,737
Kooina, fight me with the real sword.

91
00:06:39,217 --> 00:06:40,077
Real sword?

92
00:06:41,457 --> 00:06:42,497
You're on.

93
00:06:50,657 --> 00:07:04,537
And that makes 2,000 wins for me.

94
00:07:07,817 --> 00:07:10,417
Oh man, bad memories.

95
00:07:11,857 --> 00:07:13,977
All right kids, break's over.

96
00:07:14,317 --> 00:07:15,737
Time for your afternoon lessons.

97
00:07:15,917 --> 00:07:16,397
Okay.

98
00:07:16,397 --> 00:07:30,197
No, no, no, no.

99
00:07:30,277 --> 00:07:31,857
He wants to fight us.

100
00:07:34,357 --> 00:07:35,497
Hey, calm down.

101
00:07:35,677 --> 00:07:36,537
There's no need to worry.

102
00:07:36,677 --> 00:07:37,817
He didn't come here to challenge you.

103
00:07:38,077 --> 00:07:39,257
Don't you guys recognize him?

104
00:07:39,557 --> 00:07:41,197
This is the Pirate Hunter Zorro.

105
00:07:41,617 --> 00:07:42,077
What?

106
00:07:42,637 --> 00:07:43,877
That's so cool.

107
00:07:46,397 --> 00:07:53,437
Can I have your autograph?

108
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:57,977
That's just pathetic.

109
00:08:05,117 --> 00:08:05,757
Whoa.

110
00:08:07,037 --> 00:08:09,777
It's identical to the mansion Kaya lived in.

111
00:08:10,297 --> 00:08:12,357
Wow, this really takes me back.

112
00:08:13,077 --> 00:08:15,677
She would always pop her head out of the upstairs window.

113
00:08:16,397 --> 00:08:17,837
Hey, Usopp.

114
00:08:18,177 --> 00:08:19,277
Oh, hiya, Kaya.

115
00:08:21,737 --> 00:08:22,137
Nope.

116
00:08:22,417 --> 00:08:23,417
Did I keep you waiting?

117
00:08:24,757 --> 00:08:26,957
What adventure are you going to tell me about today?

118
00:08:27,437 --> 00:08:29,157
Yeah, let me think of a good one.

119
00:08:29,457 --> 00:08:34,177
Have I told you about the time I fought a giant goldfish at the South Pole when I was 5 years old?

120
00:08:34,417 --> 00:08:35,737
A giant goldfish?

121
00:08:35,897 --> 00:08:37,557
Yeah, as big as you can imagine.

122
00:08:37,817 --> 00:08:40,497
Even its poop was practically its own landmass.

123
00:08:40,497 --> 00:08:44,677
It was so big that when I landed on it, I thought it was some kind of island.

124
00:08:49,137 --> 00:08:51,197
Man, it would be so great to see her.

125
00:08:51,917 --> 00:08:52,957
Whoa, what the?

126
00:08:54,757 --> 00:08:55,737
It's a fake.

127
00:08:56,737 --> 00:09:00,097
Well, that was the popular style on Syrup Island, isn't that right?

128
00:09:00,097 --> 00:09:03,037
Luigia apparently modeled this mansion after the one she lived in.

129
00:09:03,037 --> 00:09:03,977
You call this style?

130
00:09:04,137 --> 00:09:06,317
Who in their right mind would build something like this?

131
00:09:07,117 --> 00:09:07,937
Whoa, hold on.

132
00:09:08,657 --> 00:09:11,617
If she lived in that mansion, she might be related to Kaya.

133
00:09:11,617 --> 00:09:27,757
Huh, it can't be.

134
00:09:28,217 --> 00:09:29,357
Is that Kaya?

135
00:09:36,257 --> 00:09:38,017
Come on, come on.

136
00:09:38,017 --> 00:09:38,617
Come on, come on.

137
00:09:38,817 --> 00:09:39,257
Too old.

138
00:09:41,617 --> 00:09:56,417
You're a member of the Straw Hat Pirate Group, is that right?

139
00:09:57,757 --> 00:10:00,117
Yeah, I'm the cook for the ship.

140
00:10:00,697 --> 00:10:01,837
Where did you learn to cook?

141
00:10:02,497 --> 00:10:05,237
I spent most of my youth on the original Baratier.

142
00:10:06,977 --> 00:10:08,597
You've got to be messing with me!

143
00:10:08,597 --> 00:10:09,857
Are you serious?

144
00:10:10,037 --> 00:10:11,617
You really grew up on the Baratier?

145
00:10:11,897 --> 00:10:14,257
Yeah, I guess you could say that.

146
00:10:14,337 --> 00:10:15,297
That's just incredible.

147
00:10:15,837 --> 00:10:17,077
I'm thrilled to have you here.

148
00:10:17,377 --> 00:10:19,657
Zef's cooking is one of the greatest joys of my life.

149
00:10:19,897 --> 00:10:22,277
I was actually a regular there when it first opened,

150
00:10:22,437 --> 00:10:25,137
and I've even tried to replicate his recipes for my own dishes.

151
00:10:25,357 --> 00:10:27,057
I see you're really into this.

152
00:10:27,537 --> 00:10:29,177
The building is similar too, right?

153
00:10:29,357 --> 00:10:31,777
I don't exactly have Zef's seafaring courage,

154
00:10:31,777 --> 00:10:34,337
so I figured it'd be best for me to stick it out on land.

155
00:10:34,877 --> 00:10:38,057
But I wanted to match the feel, capture the style.

156
00:10:38,417 --> 00:10:40,217
Well, go on, why don't you give it a taste?

157
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:43,057
I'd love to, but I don't actually have any money.

158
00:10:43,237 --> 00:10:44,857
Don't worry, dig in!

159
00:10:45,057 --> 00:10:45,877
Well, if you're sure.

160
00:10:46,637 --> 00:10:47,357
All right.

161
00:10:47,357 --> 00:10:54,357
Whoa, is this...

162
00:10:54,357 --> 00:11:24,337
I don't want to match the feel, but I don't want to match the feel.

163
00:11:24,357 --> 00:11:28,357
Yes!

164
00:11:45,877 --> 00:11:45,997
Yes!

165
00:11:46,157 --> 00:11:48,237
I figured out the damn geezer's recipe!

166
00:11:52,677 --> 00:11:53,777
Okay, what do you think?

167
00:11:53,777 --> 00:11:55,177
You are the expert.

168
00:11:55,417 --> 00:11:56,517
Does it taste like Zef's?

169
00:11:58,177 --> 00:11:58,737
Huh?

170
00:12:01,237 --> 00:12:02,257
It does.

171
00:12:02,517 --> 00:12:04,317
It's actually better than Zef's.

172
00:12:04,437 --> 00:12:05,617
Do you really mean that?

173
00:12:05,817 --> 00:12:06,077
Oh!

174
00:12:06,817 --> 00:12:09,417
You've just made me the happiest man alive!

175
00:12:11,917 --> 00:12:14,197
Even the cook's falling for their crap!

176
00:12:14,197 --> 00:12:25,217
Wow, you're small.

177
00:12:25,317 --> 00:12:26,877
Yeah, and you got a big mouth!

178
00:12:27,017 --> 00:12:27,817
I know you.

179
00:12:28,177 --> 00:12:29,997
You're from Syrup Village, aren't you?

180
00:12:30,237 --> 00:12:31,277
Yeah, I am.

181
00:12:31,277 --> 00:12:31,817
I figured.

182
00:12:31,817 --> 00:12:32,677
I figured.

183
00:12:32,677 --> 00:12:34,437
You're clearly Yassup's son.

184
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:36,017
You mean you know my dad?

185
00:12:36,177 --> 00:12:37,117
To an extent.

186
00:12:37,457 --> 00:12:40,457
Well, I knew his constant lies more than I really knew the man.

187
00:12:40,457 --> 00:12:41,477
You did know him!

188
00:12:41,697 --> 00:12:42,477
Wait a sec!

189
00:12:42,677 --> 00:12:46,297
Then did you actually live in Kaya's mansion in Syrup Village like they said?

190
00:12:46,297 --> 00:12:50,337
Look, don't act like you don't know what that mansion means.

191
00:12:50,557 --> 00:12:52,717
It was held up as the glory of our village.

192
00:12:53,117 --> 00:12:54,537
Everyone dreamed of living there.

193
00:12:54,957 --> 00:12:55,257
Yeah.

194
00:12:55,257 --> 00:13:00,117
I spent my whole miserable life dreaming that I might one day live in a mansion as grand

195
00:13:00,117 --> 00:13:00,697
as that one.

196
00:13:01,237 --> 00:13:05,417
And I was finally able to bring my wish to fruition when I settled on this little island.

197
00:13:06,477 --> 00:13:09,317
That means you're not related to Kaya.

198
00:13:09,637 --> 00:13:12,677
They treat me like I'm royalty here, and I like it.

199
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:15,317
I'll keep my secret unless you'd rather die.

200
00:13:15,577 --> 00:13:15,897
Right!

201
00:13:18,457 --> 00:13:20,697
Oh no, not the granny too?

202
00:13:20,697 --> 00:13:24,537
Oh, careful!

203
00:13:24,797 --> 00:13:26,237
Make sure to watch your step in here.

204
00:13:26,677 --> 00:13:28,557
Kind of a creepy path you're taking me on.

205
00:13:28,677 --> 00:13:30,077
It's really more of a labyrinth.

206
00:13:32,677 --> 00:13:34,937
It opens up onto all different parts of the island.

207
00:13:35,457 --> 00:13:36,797
Yeah, that's real neat and all.

208
00:13:36,957 --> 00:13:37,877
But how much longer?

209
00:13:38,297 --> 00:13:40,017
Oh, we're almost there.

210
00:13:45,917 --> 00:13:46,357
What?

211
00:13:46,637 --> 00:13:46,917
What?

212
00:13:47,157 --> 00:13:48,637
What in the hell is that?

213
00:13:48,637 --> 00:13:51,097
That's the official symbol of our fan club.

214
00:13:51,417 --> 00:13:54,857
We only had a poster for reference, but it's still a pretty good likeness, huh?

215
00:13:55,037 --> 00:13:58,177
I'm not bothered by the level of craftsmanship, but why is it naked?

216
00:13:58,497 --> 00:14:00,357
Oh, that was decided by popular vote.

217
00:14:00,697 --> 00:14:04,517
We felt that was most honest, but we did have to use our imagination on the front.

218
00:14:09,117 --> 00:14:10,957
You're going to put a shirt on that thing.

219
00:14:11,337 --> 00:14:11,777
Okay.

220
00:14:11,777 --> 00:14:23,817
I don't get it.

221
00:14:24,337 --> 00:14:25,537
They're so dumb.

222
00:14:25,797 --> 00:14:30,097
You and my father always protected this island, and now they let pirates on it.

223
00:14:31,477 --> 00:14:32,977
I hate those jerks.

224
00:14:33,117 --> 00:14:33,877
I hate them.

225
00:14:33,877 --> 00:14:50,937
Stop it, boss.

226
00:14:50,937 --> 00:14:51,717
It tickles.

227
00:14:53,657 --> 00:14:54,497
Enough.

228
00:14:54,657 --> 00:14:55,017
Okay.

229
00:14:55,017 --> 00:14:55,257
Hey!

230
00:14:55,257 --> 00:14:55,757
Johan!

231
00:14:55,757 --> 00:14:55,817
Uh!

232
00:15:11,457 --> 00:15:12,417
Bye!

233
00:15:13,177 --> 00:15:13,777
Bye!

234
00:15:13,917 --> 00:15:14,497
Bye!

235
00:15:15,317 --> 00:15:15,877
Bye!

236
00:15:16,737 --> 00:15:17,337
Bye!

237
00:15:17,557 --> 00:15:17,837
Bye!

238
00:15:17,857 --> 00:15:20,637
Bye!

239
00:15:20,637 --> 00:15:21,577
Bye!

240
00:15:21,817 --> 00:15:22,117
Bye!

241
00:15:22,217 --> 00:15:22,817
Bye!

242
00:15:22,857 --> 00:15:23,157
Bye!

243
00:15:23,197 --> 00:15:23,817
Bye!

244
00:15:23,857 --> 00:15:24,777
Bye!

245
00:15:24,777 --> 00:15:48,777
All right boys, look alive!

246
00:15:48,777 --> 00:15:50,777
We've got us a job to do here.

247
00:15:50,777 --> 00:15:52,777
Who knows what kind of conditions we might face,

248
00:15:52,777 --> 00:15:55,777
but we're gonna make Shiki proud and join his team.

249
00:15:55,777 --> 00:15:57,777
We've just got to nab the giant beetle

250
00:15:57,777 --> 00:15:59,777
that fled from Shiki's hideout.

251
00:15:59,777 --> 00:16:02,777
Failure is not an option, so be ready for anything.

252
00:16:02,777 --> 00:16:04,777
Comprende?

253
00:16:04,777 --> 00:16:07,777
Si!

254
00:16:07,777 --> 00:16:10,777
Didn't mean to steal your thunder, big bro.

255
00:16:10,777 --> 00:16:13,777
You are the captain, why don't you say some rousing words?

256
00:16:16,777 --> 00:16:19,777
Oh no, he's in the middle of a siesta.

257
00:16:19,777 --> 00:16:21,777
He's gonna be out for a while.

258
00:16:22,777 --> 00:16:24,777
You bastard!

259
00:16:24,777 --> 00:16:26,777
Don't do it, Vice Captain!

260
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,777
Please, do you know how dangerous it is to wake him up

261
00:16:28,777 --> 00:16:30,777
when he's in the middle of a siesta?

262
00:16:30,777 --> 00:16:31,777
Exactly.

263
00:16:31,777 --> 00:16:33,777
That is not how I want to die.

264
00:16:33,777 --> 00:16:36,777
Comprende, but this is kind of a crappy time to take a gato nap.

265
00:16:38,777 --> 00:16:41,777
Might be tough without him, but we got no choice.

266
00:16:41,777 --> 00:16:43,777
You wanna give me a battle cry?

267
00:16:43,777 --> 00:16:44,777
Hey!

268
00:16:48,777 --> 00:16:49,777
And it's done.

269
00:16:49,777 --> 00:16:51,777
Now we're set for transporting one big beetle.

270
00:16:51,777 --> 00:16:53,777
Simply remarkable.

271
00:16:53,777 --> 00:16:55,777
Why, it scarcely took you a minute to finish.

272
00:16:56,777 --> 00:16:58,777
I'm not embarrassed to acknowledge my talents,

273
00:16:58,777 --> 00:16:59,777
and that's one of them.

274
00:16:59,777 --> 00:17:00,777
